From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] feat(dev): add in-process thread sampler

Dev only, not for release builds. Not documented in OVERVIEW.md or NOTES.md;
facts below come from the code comment.

Problem: needed thread stacks of a game that stalls, without attaching a
debugger (visible to anti-debug checks).

Root cause: n/a (diagnostic).

Fix: 60 s and 150 s after the first D3D12 device, every other thread of the
process is briefly suspended, its registers and top of stack copied into
preallocated memory, then resumed. Return-address candidates in executable
module code are written as module+offset (nearest export when available) to
C:\gfx-threads.log; a TEB stack scan is the fallback when suspension fails.

Verified by: no record in OVERVIEW.md / NOTES.md.

Off switch: needs VKD3D_DIAGNOSTICS=1; VKD3D_THREAD_SAMPLER=0 disables.
